---
layout: base.njk
description: "A-XS is an independent systems studio working across language design, native software, and interfaces. Based in Algeria. Selected work is held privately and shared by request."
---

<section class="hero">
  <div class="shell hero__inner">
    <div class="hero__meta">
      <span>Independent systems studio</span>
      <span>Private archive / Vol. I</span>
      <span>{{ site.location }} <span aria-hidden="true">·</span> {{ site.coordinates }}</span>
    </div>

    <div class="hero__main">
      <div class="hero__copy">
        <div class="hero__name" aria-hidden="true">A<span class="hero__dash"></span>XS</div>
        <h1 class="hero__tagline">
          <span class="sr-only">A-XS — </span>Software, <em>built to the line.</em>
        </h1>
        <p class="hero__lede">
          Language design, native systems, and interfaces. Work is developed in private,
          measured against the line, and published only when it holds.
        </p>
        <div class="hero__actions">
          <a class="button button--accent" href="/practice/">The practice <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a>
          <a class="button" href="/archive/">The archive <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
        </div>
      </div>

      <figure class="hero__plate">
        <div class="hero__plate-frame">
          {% inlineSvg "assets/img/armillary.svg" %}
        </div>
        <figcaption class="hero__plate-caption">
          <span>Fig. 01 — Axis composition</span>
          <span>Plate / I</span>
        </figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>

    <div class="hero__foot">
      <div>
        <strong>Practice</strong>
        <span>Language design · Native systems · Interfaces</span>
      </div>
      <div>
        <strong>Status</strong>
        <span>Private archive · Open for correspondence</span>
      </div>
      <div>
        <strong>Next</strong>
        <a class="hero__scroll" href="#manifesto">Read the manifesto</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section manifesto" id="manifesto">
  <div class="shell manifesto__grid">
    <p class="manifesto__text" data-reveal>
      Most software is assembled. <em>The work here is drawn</em> — fewer layers,
      harder materials, measured results.
    </p>
    <aside class="manifesto__aside" data-reveal>
      <div>
        <strong>Position</strong>
        Independent. {{ site.location }}. Working worldwide.
      </div>
      <div>
        <strong>Method</strong>
        Private by default. Public when ready.
      </div>
      <div>
        <strong>Standard</strong>
        If it cannot be measured, it is not a claim.
      </div>
    </aside>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section" id="practice">
  <div class="shell">
    <header class="section__head">
      <span class="section__index">I</span>
      <h2 class="section__title">The practice</h2>
      <p class="section__note">
        Three disciplines. One standard: the work should hold under inspection.
      </p>
    </header>

    <ol class="practice__list">
      <li class="practice-row" data-reveal>
        <span class="practice-row__num">01</span>
        <div class="practice-row__glyph">
          {% inlineSvg "assets/img/glyph-language.svg" %}
        </div>
        <div class="practice-row__body">
          <h3>Languages &amp; runtimes</h3>
          <p>
            Grammar, type systems, code generation, and the tooling that makes a
            language usable. Built from the source up, with the edges stated.
          </p>
        </div>
        <ul class="practice-row__tags">
          <li>Grammar</li>
          <li>Type systems</li>
          <li>Codegen</li>
          <li>Tooling</li>
        </ul>
      </li>

      <li class="practice-row" data-reveal>
        <span class="practice-row__num">02</span>
        <div class="practice-row__glyph">
          {% inlineSvg "assets/img/glyph-native.svg" %}
        </div>
        <div class="practice-row__body">
          <h3>Native systems</h3>
          <p>
            C++ and Rust for Windows: small binaries, direct APIs, and predictable
            performance. The kind of software that does one job and leaves.
          </p>
        </div>
        <ul class="practice-row__tags">
          <li>C++</li>
          <li>Rust</li>
          <li>Win32</li>
          <li>Direct3D</li>
        </ul>
      </li>

      <li class="practice-row" data-reveal>
        <span class="practice-row__num">03</span>
        <div class="practice-row__glyph">
          {% inlineSvg "assets/img/glyph-interface.svg" %}
        </div>
        <div class="practice-row__body">
          <h3>Interfaces</h3>
          <p>
            Editorial interfaces and design systems for complex tools. The interface
            is not a layer over the system; it is part of how the system thinks.
          </p>
        </div>
        <ul class="practice-row__tags">
          <li>UI systems</li>
          <li>Interaction</li>
          <li>Typography</li>
          <li>Accessibility</li>
        </ul>
      </li>
    </ol>

    <div class="section__foot">
      <a class="arrow-link" href="/practice/">Read the practice <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section" id="method">
  <div class="shell">
    <header class="section__head">
      <span class="section__index">II</span>
      <h2 class="section__title">The method</h2>
      <p class="section__note">
        Not a process diagram. Four positions that decide what gets built and what gets cut.
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="principles">
      <article class="principle" data-reveal>
        <span class="principle__num">01</span>
        <h3>Measure the claim.</h3>
        <p>
          Performance, correctness, and cost are measured, recorded, and defended.
          A number without a method is decoration.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="principle" data-reveal>
        <span class="principle__num">02</span>
        <h3>Prefer the native path.</h3>
        <p>
          Fewer layers, direct APIs, small binaries. The tool should disappear into
          the work, not announce its own machinery.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="principle" data-reveal>
        <span class="principle__num">03</span>
        <h3>The interface is part of the system.</h3>
        <p>
          A compiler, a language, or a utility is only as good as the surface that
          explains it. Legibility is an engineering concern.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="principle" data-reveal>
        <span class="principle__num">04</span>
        <h3>Publish the limit, not the promise.</h3>
        <p>
          Every system has an edge. State it plainly. Hide it and the work becomes
          marketing.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="archive-band" id="archive">
  <div class="shell archive-band__inner">
    <div class="archive-band__seal">
      {% inlineSvg "assets/img/seal.svg" %}
    </div>
    <div class="archive-band__copy">
      <span class="eyebrow">III / The archive</span>
      <h2>Private by design.</h2>
      <p>
        Current work is held privately while it is being finished. Dossiers,
        technical notes, and references are available on request — with the limits
        included.
      </p>
      <div class="archive-band__actions">
        <a class="button button--accent" href="/archive/">Request the archive <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
        <a class="button" href="/contact/">Correspondence <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
      </div>
      <dl class="archive-band__ledger">
        <div>
          <dt>Cycle</dt>
          <dd>{{ site.year }}</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>Status</dt>
          <dd>In development</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>Access</dt>
          <dd>By request</dd>
        </div>
      </dl>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section studio-teaser">
  <div class="shell studio-teaser__grid">
    <div data-reveal>
      <span class="eyebrow">IV / The studio</span>
      <h2>A practice, <em>not a feed.</em></h2>
      <p>
        A-XS is an independent systems studio based in {{ site.location }}, working
        across language design, native software, and interface craft. The work is
        intentionally quiet until it is ready.
      </p>
      <div class="studio-teaser__actions">
        <a class="arrow-link" href="/studio/">Read the studio note <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="studio-teaser__plate" data-reveal>
      {% inlineSvg "assets/img/seal.svg" %}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="contact-band">
  <div class="shell">
    <span class="eyebrow">V / Correspondence</span>
    <h2>Start a <em>conversation.</em></h2>
    <div class="contact-band__links">
      {% for social in site.socials %}
        <a href="{{ social.href }}" rel="{{ social.rel }} noopener" target="_blank">{{ social.label }} <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
      {% endfor %}
      {% if site.linkedin %}
        <a href="{{ site.linkedin }}" rel="me noopener" target="_blank">LinkedIn <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
      {% endif %}
      <a href="/contact/">Contact page <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
